# Secrets Management & Credential Governance

You are operating within the `{{project_name}}` software engineering workspace.

## 1. No Committed Secrets
Never commit API keys, service account credentials, passwords, or `.env` files into source control. All `.env*` files (except `.env.example`) must be listed in `.gitignore`.

## 2. Runtime Secret Injection
In production and local environments, secrets are injected via secure credential stores (e.g. Google Cloud Secret Manager, 1Password CLI, or runtime environment variables).
